<title>INDIA: India produces 177.7 kg gold in June, below target.</title>
<headline>India produces 177.7 kg gold in June, below target.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>India produced 177.71 kg of gold in June against a target of 190 kg, a government statement said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The country produced 482.44 kg of gold in April-June compared with 380.11 kg in the same period in 1996, the statement said.</p>
<p>		June 1997		 Cumulative production</p>
<p>		 Actual		  Apr-June 97  Apr-June 96</p>
<p> BGML	 131.91		     346.71	 249.66</p>
<p> HGML	  45.80		     136.73	 130.45</p>
<p> Total	177.71		     482.44	 380.11</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures are in kg and provisional.</p>
<p>BGML: Bharat Gold Mines Limited.</p>
<p>HGML: Hutti Gold Mines Limited.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301</p>
</text>
